🧹 Data Cleaning in Pandas (Detailed Explanation)

📌 What is Data Cleaning?

Data Cleaning is the process of identifying and fixing errors, inconsistencies, and missing values in a dataset to make it accurate, consistent, and ready for analysis.

In real-world projects, 70–80% of a data analyst’s time is spent on data cleaning.

📌 Why Data Cleaning is Important?

Improves data accuracy

Ensures reliable analysis and insights

Reduces errors in reports and models

Makes data consistent and usable

Essential before visualization and machine learning

👉 Bad data = wrong business decisions

📌 Common Data Quality Problems

Missing values

Duplicate records

Incorrect data types

Inconsistent text values

Outliers

Wrong column names

Extra spaces and formatting issues
